    "q-113356": {
      "dom_id": "step-q113356",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151148/assets/4bfd5f3d064d03dc01603ba8af47bf2d75c2ec689c7068aa280b0f0ee95fbf3c.png)\n\nWhich of the line segments shown above are congruent?",
      "worked_solution": "For two segments to be congruent, they must have the same length.\n\nSo, let's determine the length of each segment in the diagram. We see that:\n\n- $AB=EF=2$ units\n\n- $CD=3$ units\n\n- $GH=4$ units\n\nTherefore, the only pair of congruent segments is $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{EF}.$",
