    "q-113378": {
      "dom_id": "step-q113378",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151148/assets/001420c2d9eea57191ce6be891e503de29ea7919af3b84ccf2d0b559c985617d.png)\n\nGiven the number line above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\overset{―}{BC}≅\\overset{―}{CD}$\n\nII. $\\overset{―}{AB}≅\\overset{―}{CD}$\n\nIII. $\\overset{―}{AC}$ is congruent to $\\overset{―}{BD}$",
      "worked_solution": "- Statement I is false. Indeed, we have that $BC=2$ units while $CD=3$ units. So, $\\overset{―}{BC}≇\\overset{―}{CD.}$\n\n- Statement II is true since $AB=CD=3$ units. So, $\\overset{―}{AB}≅\\overset{―}{CD.}$\n\n- Statement III is true since $AC=BD=5.$ So, $\\overset{―}{AC}$ is congruent to $\\overset{―}{BD}.$\n\nTherefore, only statements II and III are true.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
