      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151148/assets/101d333d2309238209b3e5ce96fdf2a6e6881e2577a2dfc0b0b0114419a938ad.png)\n\nGiven the number line above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $PQ=QR$\n\nII. $\\overset{―}{PR}≅\\overset{―}{QS}$\n\nIII. $PR=RS$",
      "worked_solution": "- Statement I is true since $PQ=QR=20$ units.\n\n- Statement II is false since $PR=40$ units, while $QS=50$ units. So, $\\overset{―}{PR}≇\\overset{―}{QS}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, we have that $PR=40$ units, while $RS=30$ units. So, $PR\\ne RS.$\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true.",
