    "q-113396": {
      "dom_id": "step-q113396",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151148/assets/41d9a3bcc715c0d5db4a910906f471695455065d198d90f3fa6d540e8cdb1c03.png)\n\nFor the diagram shown above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The segments $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and $\\overset{―}{CD}$ are congruent\n\nII. $\\overset{―}{AE}≅\\overset{―}{AB}$\n\nIII. $BD=4\\,\\text{cm}$",
      "worked_solution": "- Statement I is false. From the picture, the two segments $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and $\\overset{―}{CD}$ have different hash marks, so \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{BC}≇\\overset{―}{CD}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. According to the picture, we have that both $\\overset{―}{AE}$ and $\\overset{―}{AB}$ have the same hash marks, so\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{AE}≅\\overset{―}{AB}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. From the picture, the two $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{BD}$ have different hash marks, so \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{AB}≇\\overset{―}{BD}.\n$$\n\nHence, $AB\\ne BD,$ and since $AB=4\\,\\text{cm},$ we have $BD\\ne 4\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
