    "q-113405": {
      "dom_id": "step-q113405",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151148/assets/a94a13b06d682fe525278b529ed862cbfacecc3a97900ad54a80d66bf4971658.png)\n\nFor the diagram shown above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The segments $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{BC}$ are congruent\n\nII. $\\overset{―}{DB}≅\\overset{―}{CE}$\n\nIII. $AD=2\\,\\text{cm}$",
      "worked_solution": "- Statement I is false. From the picture, the two segments $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{BC}$ have different hash marks, so \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{AB}≇\\overset{―}{BC}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. From the picture, the two segments $\\overset{―}{DB}$ and $\\overset{―}{CE}$ have different hash marks, so \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{DB}≇\\overset{―}{CE}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. According to the picture, we have that both $\\overset{―}{AD}$ and $\\overset{―}{BC}$ have the same hash marks, so\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{AD}≅\\overset{―}{BC}.\n$$\n\nHence, $AD=BC=2\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true.",
