    "q-113408": {
      "dom_id": "step-q113408",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151148/assets/a5373ce6d1ab92c8b71feccf545a79b2515b66198ec4ffb557c9501a171b8021.png)\n\nFor the diagram shown above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The segments $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and $\\overset{―}{CE}$ are congruent\n\nII. $DC=CE$\n\nIII. $BD=3\\,\\text{cm}$",
      "worked_solution": "- Statement I is true. According to the picture, we have that both $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and $\\overset{―}{CE}$ have the same double hash marks, so\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{BC}≅\\overset{―}{CE}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. From the picture, the two segments $\\overset{―}{DC}$ and $\\overset{―}{CE}$ have different hash marks, so \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{DC}≇\\overset{―}{CE}.\n$$\n\nHence, $DC\\ne CE.$\n\n- Statement III is true. According to the picture, we have that $\\overset{―}{BD}$ and $\\overset{―}{AB}$ have the same hash marks, so \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{BD}≅\\overset{―}{AB}.\n$$\n\nHence, $BD=AB=3\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true.",
