    "q-113406": {
      "dom_id": "step-q113406",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151148/assets/63789e47ee7a429edd48100456e3c8fdb536a1f67542c27ef687e5e85553f899.png)\n\nFor the diagram shown above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The segments $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{AD}$ are congruent\n\nII. $\\overset{―}{AC}≅\\overset{―}{BC}$\n\nIII. $BE\\ne 4\\,\\text{cm}$",
      "worked_solution": "- Statement I is true. According to the picture, we have that both $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{AD}$ have the same hash marks, so\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{AB}≅\\overset{―}{AD}.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. According to the picture, we have that both $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and $\\overset{―}{BC}$ have the same double hash marks, so\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{AC}≅\\overset{―}{BC}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. From the picture, the two segments $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{BE}$ have the same hash marks, so \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{AB}≅\\overset{―}{BE}.\n$$\n\nHence, $AB=BE=4\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true.",
